IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `bta-unitholders`

-- Business Trusts Act 2004, ss 6, 10 to 12, 20, 29, 32 to 35, 40, 40A, 45, 63 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_bta.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

§ `Fixtures`

`voting down a fee increase for the trustee-manager` MEANS Conflict WITH
    `the director preferred the unitholders` IS TRUE
    `the act harmed the trustee-manager company` IS TRUE
    `the act was required by section 11` IS TRUE

`diverting an opportunity to the director's own firm` MEANS Conflict WITH
    `the director preferred the unitholders` IS FALSE
    `the act harmed the trustee-manager company` IS TRUE
    `the act was required by section 11` IS FALSE

`a decision that harmed no one` MEANS Conflict WITH
    `the director preferred the unitholders` IS TRUE
    `the act harmed the trustee-manager company` IS FALSE
    `the act was required by section 11` IS TRUE

§ `s 6`

#ASSERT `the candidate may act as trustee-manager` `a public company` FALSE
#ASSERT `the candidate may act as trustee-manager` `a non-exempt private company` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the candidate may act as trustee-manager` `an exempt private company` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the candidate may act as trustee-manager` `an individual` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the candidate may act as trustee-manager` `a limited liability partnership` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the candidate may act as trustee-manager` `a public company` TRUE

§ `ss 10, 11`

#ASSERT NOT `the director can be sued by the trustee-manager company` `voting down a fee increase for the trustee-manager`
#ASSERT `the director can be sued by the trustee-manager company` `diverting an opportunity to the director's own firm`
#ASSERT NOT `the director can be sued by the trustee-manager company` `a decision that harmed no one`

#ASSERT NOT `a unitholder may pursue a director for breach of section 11 by this route` `a direct personal action by a unitholder`
#ASSERT `a unitholder may pursue a director for breach of section 11 by this route` `an oppression application under section 41`
#ASSERT `a unitholder may pursue a director for breach of section 11 by this route` `a derivative action under section 42`

§ `s 12`

#ASSERT `the relative's interest is treated as the director's` `spouse`
#ASSERT `the relative's interest is treated as the director's` `son`
#ASSERT `the relative's interest is treated as the director's` `stepdaughter`
#ASSERT `the relative's interest is treated as the director's` `adopted son`
#ASSERT NOT `the relative's interest is treated as the director's` `parent`
#ASSERT NOT `the relative's interest is treated as the director's` `brother`

§ `ss 20, 29, 45, 63`

#ASSERT `the trustee-manager is removed` 51 49
#ASSERT NOT `the trustee-manager is removed` 50 50
#ASSERT `the trustee-manager is removed` 10 2

#ASSERT `a special resolution is passed` 75 25 21
#ASSERT NOT `a special resolution is passed` 74 26 21
#ASSERT NOT `a special resolution is passed` 80 20 14
#ASSERT `a special resolution is passed` 3 1 30

#ASSERT NOT `the exemption is valid` `a deed clause excluding liability for negligence`
#ASSERT `the exemption is valid` `a release by special resolution for a specific past act`
#ASSERT `the exemption is valid` `a release by special resolution on the trustee-manager ceasing to act`
#ASSERT NOT `the exemption is valid` `a release by ordinary resolution`

§ `ss 32 to 35`

#ASSERT `the unitholder's exposure` 50000000 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the unitholder's exposure` 50000000 2000 EQUALS 2000

#ASSERT `the distribution may be made` TRUE 2
#ASSERT NOT `the distribution may be made` TRUE 1
#ASSERT NOT `the distribution may be made` FALSE 5

